---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "AVB (Already Vaped Bud)"
letter: "A"
anchor: "avb"
category: "edibles"
---

Cannabis that has already been used in a dry herb vaporizer. AVB is brown, dry, and has significantly lower potency than fresh flower — but it's not useless. Because vaporization applies heat, AVB is already partially or fully decarboxylated, which means it can be used directly in edibles or infusions without a separate decarb step. Potency varies widely depending on the temperature and duration of the original vaporization session. Use more of it than you would fresh flower.

→ [How to Decarb Cannabis](/edibles/decarb-activate-cannabis-edibles/)
